# Language

Human source of truth: [`docs/language.md`](../../docs/language.md).

## English everywhere

Write everything you commit or post on GitHub in **English**:

- Code: identifiers, XML docs, inline comments, exception messages
- Tests: method names, Given / When / Then remarks, comments, assertion and skip messages
- Docs, `.cursor/` rules and skills, `.github/` templates
- Commit messages, PR titles and bodies, Issues, review replies

Chat with the user may be in any language. Before writing comments or docs, read [`.cursor/skills/english-writing/SKILL.md`](../skills/english-writing/SKILL.md). When a review corrects wording, add the general rule to that skill in the same change.

## Bilingual documents

These have a Japanese translation next to them. **English is the source of truth.**

| English | Japanese |
| --- | --- |
| `README.md` | `README.ja.md` |
| `CONTRIBUTING.md` | `CONTRIBUTING.ja.md` |
| `docs/design.md` | `docs/design.ja.md` |
| `docs/roadmap.md` | `docs/roadmap.ja.md` |
| `docs/conventions.md` | `docs/conventions.ja.md` |
| `docs/language.md` | `docs/language.ja.md` |

- When you change one file of a pair, change the other in the **same PR**, with the same headings in the same order
- If you cannot update the Japanese side, say so in `## Summary` and open a follow-up Issue `docs: sync <file>.ja.md`, linked in `## Related`
- A Japanese-only change must not change the meaning. Change the English file first
- Keep the language switch line at the top of both files
- Do not add a new bilingual document without adding it to the table in `docs/language.md` and `docs/language.ja.md`

## Where Japanese is allowed

Only in `*.ja.md`, the vendored `.agents/skills/natural-japanese/` (do not edit), the Japanese terminology table in the writing skill, the language switch line, and test data that is non-ASCII on purpose (with a comment saying why).
